    {
      "layout": "content",
      "id": "song-facts",
      "step": 1,
      "background_color": "#1a1a2e",
      "title": "Cat's in the Cradle",
      "body": "<ul style=\"font-size:36px;line-height:1.7\"><li>Harry Chapin wrote the song with his wife, Sandra.</li><li>It was his only number-one single, in 1974.</li><li>It sold over one million copies and went gold.</li><li>It is the sound of a parent&rsquo;s regret &mdash; the boy grows up, and he becomes just like his dad.</li></ul>",
      "notes": "Cultural impact: a father-and-son story that became iconic. Economic success: number one on the US chart and a gold record in 1974."
    },
    {
      "layout": "raw",
      "id": "verse1-listen",
      "step": 1,
      "background_color": "#1a1a2e",
      "body": "<h2 style=\"color:#fff;text-align:center;font-size:47px;margin-bottom:14px\">First listen &mdash; What is the song about?</h2><div style=\"display:flex;align-items:center;gap:36px;justify-content:center\"><div style=\"flex:1;max-width:560px\"><p style=\"color:#fff;font-size:38px;margin:0 0 8px 0\">Watch the first verse. Don't write anything.</p><p style=\"color:#fff;font-size:38px;margin:0 0 10px 0\">The song is mainly about&hellip;</p><table style=\"width:100%;border-collapse:collapse\"><tr><td style=\"padding:8px 12px 8px 0;border-bottom:1px solid #444;width:36px;text-align:center;vertical-align:middle\"><span style=\"color:#ffdd00;font-weight:700;font-size:36px\">A</span></td><td style=\"padding:8px 0;border-bottom:1px solid #444;color:#fff;font-size:36px\">A father who always finds time for his son.</td></tr><tr><td style=\"padding:8px 12px 8px 0;border-bottom:1px solid #444;width:36px;text-align:center;vertical-align:middle\"><span style=\"color:#ffdd00;font-weight:700;font-size:36px\">B</span></td><td style=\"padding:8px 0;border-bottom:1px solid #444;color:#fff;font-size:36px\">A father who is too busy for his son.</td></tr><tr><td style=\"padding:8px 12px 8px 0;border-bottom:1px solid #444;width:36px;text-align:center;vertical-align:middle\"><span style=\"color:#ffdd00;font-weight:700;font-size:36px\">C</span></td><td style=\"padding:8px 0;border-bottom:1px solid #444;color:#fff;font-size:36px\">A son who is angry with his father.</td></tr></table></div><div style=\"flex:1;max-width:600px;text-align:center\"><iframe width=\"600\" height=\"338\" src=\"https://www.youtube-nocookie.com/embed/etundhQa724?start=64&amp;end=113\" title=\"Cat's in the Cradle\" frameborder=\"0\" allow=\"accelerometer; autoplay; clipboard-write; encrypted-media; gyroscope; picture-in-picture\" allowfullscreen></iframe></div></div>",
      "notes": "Play the first verse only. Students choose the main idea. Answer: B — a father who is too busy for his son."
    },
    {
      "layout": "content",
      "id": "verse1-answer",
      "step": 1,
      "background_color": "#052e0d",
      "title": "Answer",
      "body": "<table style=\"width:100%;border-collapse:collapse\"><tr><td style=\"padding:8px 12px 8px 0;border-bottom:1px solid #444;font-weight:700;color:#ffdd00;white-space:nowrap;vertical-align:top;width:90px\">Answer</td><td style=\"padding:8px 0;border-bottom:1px solid #444\">B &mdash; A father who is too busy for his son.</td></tr><tr><td style=\"padding:8px 12px 8px 0;font-weight:700;color:#ffdd00;white-space:nowrap;vertical-align:top\">Why</td><td style=\"padding:8px 0\">The father has planes to catch and bills to pay. He learns to walk while he is away.</td></tr></table>",
      "notes": "Confirm B. The father is absent — he is always busy with work."
    },
    {
      "layout": "raw",
      "id": "gapfill-task",
      "step": 1,
      "background_color": "#1a1a2e",
      "body": "<h2 style=\"color:#fff;text-align:center;font-size:47px;margin-bottom:14px\">Complete the gaps</h2><p style=\"color:#fff;text-align:center;font-size:38px;margin:0 0 8px 0\">Open your worksheet to the Entry Ticket.</p><p style=\"color:#fff;text-align:center;font-size:38px;margin:0 0 20px 0\">Listen to the rest of the song <strong>once</strong> and fill in the gaps.</p><div style=\"text-align:center\"><iframe width=\"880\" height=\"495\" src=\"https://www.youtube-nocookie.com/embed/etundhQa724?start=114\" title=\"Cat's in the Cradle\" frameborder=\"0\" allow=\"accelerometer; autoplay; clipboard-write; encrypted-media; gyroscope; picture-in-picture\" allowfullscreen></iframe></div>",
      "notes": "Play the whole song once. Students fill the 25 gaps on the worksheet. Check answers afterwards."
